## Model Architecture

**Model:** `SGDRegressor` (Scikit-learn) — Stochastic Gradient Descent Regressor

**Why SGD and not Ridge/LinearRegression:**
- Ridge gives a single-shot closed-form solution — you can't do round-by-round training with it
- SGD uses iterative gradient updates, which means each round of federated training genuinely improves the model
- This gives us **real convergence curves** showing MAE decreasing round by round

**Scaling:** Both X (features) and y (target) are standardised using `StandardScaler` before training. The y scaler's mean and scale are stored in the model parameters so predictions can be inverse-transformed back to real ridership numbers.

**Target variable:** `MonthTotal` — total monthly rides per route

